processes/optical                                op-V11-02-00
-----------------
- G4OpBoundaryProcess: correctly calculate Fresnel reflection/refraction,    (*)
  when material property TRANSMITTANCE is specified. The ratio of Fresnel
  reflection/refraction now does not change when a non-zero transmission is
  specified. Previously, if transmission of X% was specified, there would be
  transmission of X% as expected, but the ratio of Fresnel refraction to
  Fresnel reflection would be set to X%. Addressing problem report #2578.

run                                              run-V11-02-08
---
- First full implementation of of sub-event parallelism, adding the creation
  and processing of sub-events in workers, plus the merging of results back
  into events on the main thread. Some additional work may be needed to
  correctly retain a limited sample of events.
  No impact of the core changes needed to support sub event parallelism in
  any other mode (Seq, MT, Tasking) other than some counting issues with
  retained events.
- Added call in G4WorkerRunManager to use parallel initialisation of voxels.
- In G4RunManager::ReinitializeGeometry(), added call to new function
  G4FieldBuilder::Reinitialize().

